# ATO contextual learning

In Linux/WSL only, follow the installed global `contextual-learning` skill
when the global workflow applies. Read current `docs/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md`, including
its post-fix checklist; verify architecture, versions, environment and exclusions
before reusing a lesson. Preserve requested verification scope and explain any
necessary check that was not run. Keep app commands and exceptions local; do not
create a second lesson store or copy shared policy. If global tooling is missing,
report the limit and continue only with authorized project contracts and checks.
New or changed global skills/rules require the user's authorization; retained
lessons cannot expand permissions or weaken safeguards.
